# {{phonetic alphabet|NATO/ICAO=1|ITU/IMO=1|word=1|00}}

====Usage notes====
Used only for whole hundreds (a final 00 in a number), and then only for distances (including altitudes). Thus <span style="color:green">10,9'''00''' m</span> is ''one zero thousand nine '''hundred''' meter'', but <span style="color:red">10,946 m</span> is ''one zero thousand nine four six meter'' and <span style="color:red">200°</span> is ''two zero zero degree''.

